.TH INTEGRATION-INSTALL 1 "July 2026" "SPP Framework" "SPP CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
integration:install \- Automates the scaffolding and routing of an external application within the SPP environment.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php spp.php integration:install
.IR <app_name>
.IR <route_path>
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B integration:install
command is the foundational tool for establishing a local Data Mesh. When you want to run a monolithic application (like WordPress or Magento) on the same server as your SPP framework, this command provisions the necessary infrastructure.
.PP
It automatically performs three critical steps:
.br
1. Filesystem Scaffolding: It creates a physical directory in the public folder corresponding to the requested route.
.br
2. Route Bypassing: It modifies etc/routes.yml to instruct the SPP router to ignore this path.
.br
3. Driver Instantiation: It prepares the internal IntegrationFactory driver with the absolute local path.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B app_name
The alias of the registered driver (e.g., wordpress, moodle, magento).
.TP
.B route_path
The web-accessible path where the app will live (e.g., /blog, /lms).
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
.B Filesystem Writes:
Creates directories via mkdir() in the /public root. Appends bypass configuration strings to etc/routes.yml.
.br
.B DB Interactions:
None.
.br
.B Outbound HTTP Calls:
None.
